{title: House of the Rising Sun}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: intermediate}
{tags: folk, blues, ballad}
{comment: Let each chord ring: pick the strings one at a time, low to high, or strum down-down-up.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There [Am]is a [C]house in [D]New Or[F]leans
They [Am]call the [C]Rising [E]Sun [E]
And it's [Am]been the [C]ruin of [D]many a poor [F]girl
And [Am]me, oh [E]Lord, for [Am]one [E]

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If [Am]I had [C]listened [D]what Mama [F]said
I'd [Am]be at [C]home to[E]day [E]
But [Am]being so [C]young and [D]foolish, poor [F]girl
I [Am]let a [E]gambler lead me a[Am]stray [E]

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Go [Am]tell my [C]baby [D]sister [F]
Never [Am]do what [C]I have [E]done [E]
But [Am]shun that [C]house in [D]New Or[F]leans
They [Am]call the [E]Rising [Am]Sun [Am]
